      <td width="38%" valign="top" height="192"> 
        <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif"><b>PMWATCH/NAAJA</b> 
          -- July 24, 2002 -- Part and parcel of our struggle to promote the Palestinian 
          narrative in the US mainstream media is the effort to foster and push 
          greater presence of Arab and Muslim voices, along with voices of those 
          who speak for justice and peace in the Middle East. Toward this goal, 
          <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/index.html" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">Palestine Media Watch</a> (PMWATCH) 
          is forging a working alliance with <a href="http://www.hanania.com/caajc/caajc.htm" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">The 
          National Arab American Journalists Association</a> (NAAJA) to encourage 
          the establishment of local chapters of <a href="http://www.hanania.com/caajc/caajc.htm" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">NAAJA</a> 
          in all the major US cities and beyond. With <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/index.html" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">PMWatch</a>'s 
          ability to mobilize at the grassroots level and <a href="http://www.hanania.com/caajc/caajc.htm" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">NAAJA</a>'s 
          solid infrastructure, we hope to establish a vibrant and thriving network 
          of journalists and writers dedicated to speaking on issues of concern 
          to the Arab and Muslim communities in the United States.</font></p>
        <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">If you are interested 
          in joining <a href="http://www.hanania.com/caajc/caajc.htm" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">NAAJA</a> 
          or in establishing a chapter in your city, please fill the interface 
          below and click "send". Your information will be sent to <a href="http://www.hanania.com/caajc/caajc.htm" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">NAAJA</a>.</font></p>
    </td></tr>
